<title>USA: Video Sentry sells surveillance system.</title>
<headline>Video Sentry sells surveillance system.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Video Sentry Corp said Thursday it sold a SentryVision surveillance system to be installed in the U.S. Postal Service Sugarhouse Facility, a mail-sorting operation in Chicago.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>&quot;This is our first U.S. Postal Service installation,&quot; Andrew Benson, president, said in a statement.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
